IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the member of a super fund
-- meets: eligibility age (s 10); when an amount in my fund is "unclaimed money" and my fund's duty to try to reach me (ss 12,
-- 13, 14, 15); when my account is an inactive low-balance account (s 20QA) or a lost member account (s 24B); whether I am a
-- former temporary resident (s 20AA); by when my fund must pay my money to the Commissioner (ss 17(1), 20E(2), 20F(1), 20QD(1),
-- 21C(2), 22, 24E(1)); whom the Commissioner must pay it back to, and whether interest comes with it (ss 17(1C)-(2AE), 20H,
-- 20QF, 21E, 22B, 24G); the transfer to my active account (s 24NA); getting an overpayment back from me (ss 20L, 20QK, 21G,
-- 22E, 24K, 24NAA); and objecting (s 20P).
--
-- SEAT: the member of a superannuation fund, approved deposit fund or RSA (s 8 "member"), and, where a member has died, the
-- person entitled to the benefit; for s 12(2), the non-member spouse entitled under a payment split. "Is my super lost or
-- unclaimed? When must my fund hand it to the ATO? How do I get it back?" Duties addressed to the superannuation provider or
-- the Commissioner are encoded as what they mean for that person: what my fund must do and by when, and whom the Commissioner
-- must pay.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 42, compilation date 28 September 2022, includes amendments up to Act No. 127, 2021 (register id
-- C2022C00273), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00518.txt. No instrument is deposited: the unclaimed money
-- days and scheduled statement days (the Commissioner's instruments under ss 15A and 20B) are INPUTS; the interest the
-- regulations work out is not computed; prescribed visas, prescribed conditions of release, the "prescribed period" of
-- s 24NA(2)(c) and the KiwiSaver "prescribed matters" are asked as facts. The Act's own eligibility ages (65 and 60, s 10(1))
-- are used; an age prescribed by the regulations would change the answers (NOTES.md).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The statements themselves and their errors (ss 16, 16A, 20E(1), 20QB, 20QC, 21A, 21B, 22A, 24C, 24D) beyond
-- their due days; the amount formulas lost in conversion (s 17(1A), the death-beneficiary shares of ss 17(2AA), 20H(4), 20QF(4),
-- 21E(4), 22B(4), 24G(3): `not covered` where there is more than one death beneficiary); the s 20F(2)-(4) amount; State and
-- Territory and prescribed public sector schemes (ss 18, 18AA, 20JA, 20QG, 20QH, 22D, 24H, 24HA); refunds to and repayments
-- by providers (ss 18A, 18C, 20K, 20M, 20QJ, 20QL, 21F, 21H, 22C, 22F, 24J, 24L, 24NB); revocation of a s 20C notice (s 20J)
-- except as a decision I may object to; registers, tax file numbers, records, offences' penalty amounts and the machinery
-- (Parts 1, 5, 6, ss 19, 20, 20N, 23, 24, 24M, 40-50). The s 24NA(3) case of more than one eligible fund answers
-- `not covered`.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the member's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 -- the member's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the death-beneficiary formula is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so a share cannot be worked out where there is more than one death beneficiary`
    `more than one fund meets s 24NA(2)(b) to (e), so the Commissioner pays as the regulations provide (s 24NA(3)), and the regulations are not deposited`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 10 -- my eligibility age`

-- s 10(1): "eligibility age means: (a) in the case of a man--65 years or, if another age is prescribed by the regulations, the
-- age so prescribed; or (b) in the case of a woman--60 years or, if another age is prescribed by the regulations, the age so
-- prescribed." (2)(a): "if the superannuation provider does not know whether the member is a man or a woman--the member is
-- taken to be a man". (2)(b): if it does not know the date of birth it may determine an age (it "turned 18" on joining, on the
-- first amount received, or at the start of the eligible service period), so the age asked is the age as the fund knows or
-- determines it. No regulation is deposited: the Act's own 65 and 60 are used (NOTES.md finding 1).
DECLARE `What my fund knows of my sex` IS ONE OF
    `my fund knows I am a man`
    `my fund knows I am a woman`
    `my fund does not know whether I am a man or a woman`

GIVEN `what my fund knows` IS A `What my fund knows of my sex`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the eligibility age for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what my fund knows`
    WHEN `my fund knows I am a woman` THEN 60
    WHEN `my fund knows I am a man` THEN 65
    WHEN `my fund does not know whether I am a man or a woman` THEN 65

@export What is my eligibility age under s 10 of the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act?
GIVEN `what my fund knows` IS A `What my fund knows of my sex` @desc Whether your fund knows you are a man, knows you are a woman, or does not know (it then treats you as a man)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my eligibility age` MEANS `the eligibility age for me` `what my fund knows`

GIVEN `what my fund knows` IS A `What my fund knows of my sex`
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I have reached the eligibility age` IF
    `my age` AT LEAST `the eligibility age for me` `what my fund knows`

§§ `ss 12, 13 -- is my super unclaimed money`

-- s 12(1): "An amount payable to a member of a fund is taken to be unclaimed money if: (a) the member has reached the
-- eligibility age; and (c) the superannuation provider has not received an amount in respect of the member (and, in the case
-- of a defined benefits superannuation scheme, no benefit has accrued in respect of the member) within the last 2 years; and
-- (d) after the end of a period of 5 years since the superannuation provider last had contact with the member, the provider
-- has been unable to contact the member again after making reasonable efforts." (There is no paragraph (b).)
-- s 13(1): the provider "must make reasonable efforts to contact a member" if "(a) paragraphs 12(1)(a) and (c) are satisfied
-- ... and (b) 5 years have passed since the provider last had contact with the member". (2): an offence, 100 penalty units.
-- "within the last 2 years" is asked as complete months since the fund last received an amount for me: 24 or more means
-- nothing within the last 2 years.
GIVEN `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER
      `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `nothing received or accrued for me within the last 2 years` IF
        `months since an amount was received` AT LEAST 24
    AND (NOT `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years`)

DECLARE `Is my super unclaimed money` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is unclaimed money (s 12(1)), and my fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
    `not yet: but my fund must make reasonable efforts to contact me (s 13(1))`
    `no: it is not unclaimed money under s 12(1)`

@export Is the money my super fund holds for me "unclaimed money" under s 12(1), and must my fund try to contact me (s 13)?
GIVEN `what my fund knows` IS A `What my fund knows of my sex` @desc Whether your fund knows you are a man, knows you are a woman, or does not know
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in complete years, as your fund knows it or has determined it under s 10(2)(b) if it does not know your date of birth
      `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months since your fund last received any amount for you (a contribution, a rollover or anything else)
      `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a defined benefits scheme: whether any benefit has accrued for you within the last 2 years (answer no for an ordinary accumulation account)
      `years since last contact` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete years since your fund last had contact with you
      `my fund cannot reach me after reasonable efforts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fund, after making reasonable efforts since those 5 years ended, has been unable to contact you again
GIVETH AN `Is my super unclaimed money`
`Is my super unclaimed money (s 12)` MEANS
    IF      `I have reached the eligibility age` `what my fund knows` `my age`
        AND `nothing received or accrued for me within the last 2 years` `months since an amount was received` `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years`
        AND `years since last contact` AT LEAST 5
    THEN IF `my fund cannot reach me after reasonable efforts`
         THEN `yes: it is unclaimed money (s 12(1)), and my fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
         ELSE `not yet: but my fund must make reasonable efforts to contact me (s 13(1))`
    ELSE `no: it is not unclaimed money under s 12(1)`

§§ `ss 12(2), 13(1A) -- my share under a family law payment split`

-- s 12(2): "If: (a) a payment split applies to a splittable payment in respect of an interest that a person has as a member of
-- a fund; and (b) as a result, the non-member spouse ... is entitled to be paid an amount; and (c) after making reasonable
-- efforts and after a reasonable period has passed, the superannuation provider concerned is unable to ensure that the
-- non-member spouse ... receives the amount; then the amount payable is taken to be unclaimed money." s 13(1A): "If paragraphs
-- 12(2)(a) and (b) are satisfied, the superannuation provider must make reasonable efforts to ensure that the non-member
-- spouse ... receives the amount." No age applies to the non-member spouse.
DECLARE `Is my payment split amount unclaimed money` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the amount is unclaimed money (s 12(2)), and the fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
    `not yet: but the fund must make reasonable efforts to ensure that I receive it (s 13(1A))`
    `no: s 12(2) does not apply, because no payment split entitles me to be paid an amount`

@export I am the non-member spouse under a family law superannuation split. Is my amount unclaimed money (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `a payment split entitles me to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a payment split under Part VIIIB or VIIIC of the Family Law Act 1975 applies to your former partner's super and, as a result, you are entitled to be paid an amount
      `the fund cannot ensure I receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after making reasonable efforts and after a reasonable period has passed, the fund has been unable to ensure you receive the amount
GIVETH AN `Is my payment split amount unclaimed money`
`Is my payment split amount unclaimed money (s 12(2))` MEANS
    IF `a payment split entitles me to be paid`
    THEN IF `the fund cannot ensure I receive it`
         THEN `yes: the amount is unclaimed money (s 12(2)), and the fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
         ELSE `not yet: but the fund must make reasonable efforts to ensure that I receive it (s 13(1A))`
    ELSE `no: s 12(2) does not apply, because no payment split entitles me to be paid an amount`

§§ `ss 14, 15 -- a member who has died`

-- (Situation: a member has died and I am, or may be, the person entitled to the benefit.)
-- s 14: "An amount payable in respect of a member of a fund is taken to be unclaimed money if: (a) the member has died; and
-- (b) the superannuation provider determines that ... a benefit (other than a pension or annuity) is immediately payable in
-- respect of the member; and (c) the superannuation provider has not received an amount in respect of the member (and, in
-- the case of a defined benefits superannuation scheme, no benefit has accrued ...) within the last 2 years; and (d) after
-- making reasonable efforts and after a reasonable period has passed, the superannuation provider is unable to ensure that the
-- benefit is received by the person who is entitled to receive the benefit." s 15(1): if (a), (b) and (c) are satisfied the
-- provider "must make reasonable efforts to ensure that the person entitled to receive the benefit does receive the benefit".
-- The fund's determination under (b) is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Is the dead member's benefit unclaimed money` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the benefit is unclaimed money (s 14), and the fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
    `not yet: but the fund must make reasonable efforts to ensure that the person entitled receives it (s 15(1))`
    `no: s 14 does not apply to this benefit`

@export A member of a super fund has died and I may be entitled to the benefit. Is it unclaimed money (s 14), and what must the fund do (s 15)?
GIVEN `the fund has determined a lump sum is immediately payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has determined that, under its rules or by law, a benefit other than a pension or annuity is immediately payable because of the member's death
      `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months since the fund last received any amount for the member
      `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a defined benefits scheme: whether any benefit accrued for the member within the last 2 years (answer no for an ordinary accumulation account)
      `the fund cannot ensure the person entitled receives it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after making reasonable efforts and after a reasonable period has passed, the fund has been unable to ensure that the person entitled receives the benefit
GIVETH AN `Is the dead member's benefit unclaimed money`
`Is the dead member's benefit unclaimed money (s 14)` MEANS
    IF      `the fund has determined a lump sum is immediately payable`
        AND `nothing received or accrued for me within the last 2 years` `months since an amount was received` `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years`
    THEN IF `the fund cannot ensure the person entitled receives it`
         THEN `yes: the benefit is unclaimed money (s 14), and the fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
         ELSE `not yet: but the fund must make reasonable efforts to ensure that the person entitled receives it (s 15(1))`
    ELSE `no: s 14 does not apply to this benefit`

§§ `s 20QA -- is my account an inactive low-balance account`

-- s 20QA(1)(a), for a regulated superannuation fund: "(i) the fund has 7 or more members; and (ii) the account is held on
-- behalf of a member ...; and (iii) the account relates, in whole or in part, to a MySuper product or choice product held by
-- that member; and (iv) the superannuation provider has not received an amount in respect of the member for crediting to that
-- product within the last 16 months; and (v) the balance of the account that relates to that product is less than $6,000; and
-- (vi) the member has not satisfied any of the conditions of release ... prescribed ...; and (vii) the account does not support
-- or relate to a defined benefit interest ...; and (viii)-(x)" no benefit under the product is provided by insurance under the
-- SIS Act's ss 68AAA, 68AAB or 68AAC exceptions. (1)(b), for an RSA or approved deposit fund: held for a member, nothing
-- received "within the last 16 months", balance "less than $6,000", no prescribed condition of release, no defined benefit
-- interest. (1A): an account in a regulated superannuation fund "is taken not to be" one if in the last 16 months the member
-- "(i) changed the member's investment options ...; (ii) made changes in relation to the member's insurance coverage ...;
-- (iii) made or amended a binding beneficiary nomination; (iv) ... made an election that the account was not an inactive
-- low-balance account." The prescribed conditions of release and the insurance exceptions are asked as facts.
DECLARE `Kind of fund` IS ONE OF
    `a regulated superannuation fund`
    `an RSA (retirement savings account)`
    `an approved deposit fund`

@export Is my super account an "inactive low-balance account" that my fund must send to the ATO (s 20QA)?
GIVEN `kind of fund` IS A `Kind of fund` @desc What kind of fund holds the account: a regulated superannuation fund (most super funds), an RSA, or an approved deposit fund
      `the fund has 7 or more members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a regulated superannuation fund: whether it has 7 or more members (a self managed fund has fewer)
      `it is a MySuper or choice product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a regulated superannuation fund: whether the account relates, in whole or part, to a MySuper or choice product you hold
      `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months since the fund last received an amount for you (for that product)
      `the balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The balance of the account (for that product) in dollars
      `I have met a prescribed condition of release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have satisfied a condition of release of benefits that the regulations prescribe for s 20QA (for example retirement after preservation age, if prescribed)
      `it supports a defined benefit interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account supports or relates to a defined benefit interest
      `insurance is provided under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a regulated superannuation fund: whether any benefit under the product is provided by insurance that the SIS Act's ss 68AAA, 68AAB or 68AAC exceptions allow
      `I acted on the account in the last 16 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a regulated superannuation fund: whether in the last 16 months you changed investment options or insurance, made or amended a binding beneficiary nomination, or told the fund in writing it is not an inactive low-balance account
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my account an inactive low-balance account` IF
    CONSIDER `kind of fund`
    WHEN `a regulated superannuation fund` THEN
            `the fund has 7 or more members`
        AND `it is a MySuper or choice product`
        AND `months since an amount was received` AT LEAST 16
        AND `the balance` LESS THAN 6000
        AND (NOT `I have met a prescribed condition of release`)
        AND (NOT `it supports a defined benefit interest`)
        AND (NOT `insurance is provided under it`)
        AND (NOT `I acted on the account in the last 16 months`)
    OTHERWISE
            `months since an amount was received` AT LEAST 16
        AND `the balance` LESS THAN 6000
        AND (NOT `I have met a prescribed condition of release`)
        AND (NOT `it supports a defined benefit interest`)

§§ `s 24B -- is my account a lost member account`

-- s 8: "lost member means a member of a fund who is: (a) a lost RSA holder within the meaning of the Retirement Savings
-- Accounts Regulations 1997; or (b) a lost member within the meaning of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations
-- 1994" (a borrowed term, asked as a fact). s 24B(1) small accounts: "(a) the member ... is a lost member; and (b) the balance
-- of the account is less than $6,000; and (c) the account does not support or relate to a defined benefit interest". (2)
-- inactive accounts of unidentifiable members: "(a) ... a lost member; and (b) the superannuation provider has not received an
-- amount in respect of the member within the last 12 months; and (c) the superannuation provider is satisfied that it will
-- never be possible for the provider ... to pay an amount to the member; and (d)" no defined benefit interest.
DECLARE `Is my account a lost member account` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a small account of a lost member (s 24B(1))`
    `yes: an inactive account of an unidentifiable lost member (s 24B(2))`
    `no: it is not a lost member account under s 24B`

@export Is my super account a "lost member account" that my fund must send to the ATO (s 24B)?
GIVEN `I am a lost member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a "lost member" under the SIS Regulations 1994 (or a lost RSA holder under the RSA Regulations 1997), for example because the fund's mail to you has come back and you have not been in touch
      `the balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The balance of the account in dollars
      `it supports a defined benefit interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account supports or relates to a defined benefit interest
      `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months since the fund last received an amount for you
      `the fund is satisfied it can never pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund is satisfied that, on the information reasonably available to it, it will never be possible to pay you an amount
GIVETH AN `Is my account a lost member account`
`Is my account a lost member account (s 24B)` MEANS
    IF `I am a lost member` AND (NOT `it supports a defined benefit interest`)
    THEN IF `the balance` LESS THAN 6000
         THEN `yes: a small account of a lost member (s 24B(1))`
         ELSE IF `months since an amount was received` AT LEAST 12 AND `the fund is satisfied it can never pay me`
              THEN `yes: an inactive account of an unidentifiable lost member (s 24B(2))`
              ELSE `no: it is not a lost member account under s 24B`
    ELSE `no: it is not a lost member account under s 24B`

§§ `s 20AA -- am I a former temporary resident`

-- (Situation: I held a temporary visa and have left Australia.)
-- s 20AA(1): "a person is a former temporary resident if: (a) ... the person: (i) was ... the holder of a temporary visa,
-- except a visa prescribed under subsection (2) ..., that has ceased to be in effect; and (ii) left Australia after starting to
-- be the holder of the visa ...; and (b) at least 6 months have passed since the later of the following events ...: (i) the
-- visa ceased to be in effect; (ii) the person left Australia; and (c) the person: (i) is not ... the holder of a temporary
-- visa or permanent visa; and (ii) is neither an Australian citizen nor a New Zealand citizen; and (iii) has not made a valid
-- application for a permanent visa that has not been finally determined". The 6 months are asked as complete months since the
-- later event.
@export I held a temporary visa and have left Australia. Am I a "former temporary resident" whose super goes to the ATO (s 20AA)?
GIVEN `my temporary visa has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958 that has now ceased to be in effect
      `it is a prescribed visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that visa is one the regulations prescribe as excluded from s 20AA
      `I left Australia after it began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you left Australia after you started to hold that visa
      `months since the later event` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have passed since the later of the visa ceasing and your leaving Australia
      `I now hold an Australian visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now hold a temporary or permanent visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am an Australian or New Zealand citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen or a New Zealand citizen
      `my permanent visa application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a valid application for a permanent visa that has not been finally determined
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a former temporary resident` IF
        `my temporary visa has ceased`
    AND (NOT `it is a prescribed visa`)
    AND `I left Australia after it began`
    AND `months since the later event` AT LEAST 6
    AND (NOT `I now hold an Australian visa`)
    AND (NOT `I am an Australian or New Zealand citizen`)
    AND (NOT `my permanent visa application is pending`)

§§ `ss 17(1), 20E, 20F, 20QD, 21C, 22, 24E -- by when must my fund pay it to the Commissioner`

-- s 17(1) (unclaimed money), s 20QD(1) (inactive low-balance account), s 24E(1) (lost member account): the amount "is due and
-- payable at the end of the scheduled statement day for the unclaimed money day". Both days are set by the Commissioner's
-- legislative instrument (s 15A), not deposited: an input.
-- s 20F(1) (former temporary resident, after a s 20C notice): due "at the end of: (a) the next scheduled statement day after
-- the notice is given; or (b) if the Commissioner gives the notice less than 28 days before the next scheduled statement
-- day--the following scheduled statement day; or (c) if a day is identified for the superannuation provider under the
-- regulations that is later ...--that later day." s 20E(2) sets the same day for the statement. Scheduled statement days are
-- set under s 20B (an input). "less than 28 days before": the notice day plus 28 falls after the next scheduled statement day.
-- s 21C(2) (eligible rollover fund): "(a) 30 June 2021, if the account is an ERF low balance account; or (b) 31 January 2022,
-- if the account is not". s 21A(1)(a)(ii): an ERF low balance account had "a balance of less than $6,000" at the end of 1 June
-- 2021.
-- s 22(1): a provider "may pay" an amount it holds for me if "it reasonably believes that paying the amount to the
-- Commissioner would be in the best interests of" me: no day, and no duty.
DECLARE `Why my fund pays the Commissioner` IS ONE OF
    `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))`
    `my account is an inactive low-balance account (s 20QD(1))`
    `my account is a lost member account (s 24E(1))`
    `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)`
    `my account is in an eligible rollover fund (s 21C)`
    `my fund chooses to pay because it believes it is in my best interests (s 22)`

DECLARE `When my fund must pay the Commissioner` IS ONE OF
    `by the end of` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no day: my fund may pay the Commissioner under s 22 but is not required to`

@export By when must my super fund pay my money to the Commissioner (the ATO)?
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why my fund pays the Commissioner` @desc Why your money is going to the Commissioner: unclaimed money, an inactive low-balance account, a lost member account, a former temporary resident notice, an eligible rollover fund account, or a voluntary payment by your fund
      `the scheduled statement day` IS A DATE @desc For unclaimed money, inactive low-balance and lost member accounts: the scheduled statement day the Commissioner has set for the unclaimed money day on which your money qualified (ignored otherwise)
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc For a former temporary resident: the day the Commissioner gave your fund the s 20C notice about you (ignored otherwise)
      `the next scheduled statement day after the notice` IS A DATE @desc For a former temporary resident: the next scheduled statement day the Commissioner has set under s 20B after the notice (ignored otherwise)
      `the scheduled statement day after that` IS A DATE @desc For a former temporary resident: the scheduled statement day after that one (ignored otherwise)
      `a later day is identified under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a former temporary resident: whether a later day has been identified for your fund under the regulations for s 20F(1)(c) (answer no if you do not know of one)
      `the later day` IS A DATE @desc For a former temporary resident: that later day, if one is identified (ignored otherwise)
      `my ERF balance was under $6,000 on 1 June 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an eligible rollover fund account: whether its balance at the end of 1 June 2021 was less than $6,000 (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A `When my fund must pay the Commissioner`
`By when must my fund pay the Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))` THEN `by the end of` `the scheduled statement day`
    WHEN `my account is an inactive low-balance account (s 20QD(1))` THEN `by the end of` `the scheduled statement day`
    WHEN `my account is a lost member account (s 24E(1))` THEN `by the end of` `the scheduled statement day`
    WHEN `the Commissioner has given my fund a notice that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` THEN
        `by the end of` (`the s 20F due day` `the day of the notice` `the next scheduled statement day after the notice` `the scheduled statement day after that` `a later day is identified under the regulations` `the later day`)
    WHEN `my account is in an eligible rollover fund (s 21C)` THEN
        IF `my ERF balance was under $6,000 on 1 June 2021`
        THEN `by the end of` (Date 30 6 2021)
        ELSE `by the end of` (Date 31 1 2022)
    WHEN `my fund chooses to pay because it believes it is in my best interests (s 22)` THEN `no day: my fund may pay the Commissioner under s 22 but is not required to`

GIVEN `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the next scheduled statement day after the notice` IS A DATE
      `the scheduled statement day after that` IS A DATE
      `a later day is identified under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 20F due day` MEANS
    IF `a later day is identified under the regulations` AND `the later day` GREATER THAN `the day under (a) or (b)`
    THEN `the later day`
    ELSE `the day under (a) or (b)`
    WHERE
        `the day under (a) or (b)` MEANS
            IF (`the day of the notice` PLUS 28) GREATER THAN `the next scheduled statement day after the notice`
            THEN `the scheduled statement day after that`
            ELSE `the next scheduled statement day after the notice`

§§ `ss 17(1C)-(2AAB), 20QF, 21E, 22B, 24G -- whom must the Commissioner pay my money to`

-- s 17(1C): the Commissioner pays where "(b) the Commissioner is satisfied, on application in the approved form or on the
-- Commissioner's own initiative, that it is possible for the Commissioner to pay the unclaimed money in accordance with
-- subsection (2)". s 17(2): "(a) to a single fund if: (i) the person has not died; and (ii) the person directs the Commissioner
-- to pay to the fund; and (iii) the fund is a complying superannuation plan ...; or (aa) to a single KiwiSaver scheme provider
-- if: (i) the person has not died; and (ii) the person directs ...; and (iii) the matters (if any) prescribed by the
-- regulations are satisfied; or (b) in accordance with subsection (2AA) if: (i) the person has died; and (ii) the Commissioner
-- is satisfied that ... the provider would have been required to pay ... death benefits to one or more other persons (death
-- beneficiaries) ...; or (c) to the person's legal personal representative if the person has died but subparagraph (b)(ii)
-- does not apply; or (d) in any other case--to the person."
-- (2AAA): "Despite paragraph (2)(a), the Commissioner must not pay ... to a single fund if the unclaimed money includes a New
-- Zealand-sourced amount and either: (a) the fund is a self managed superannuation fund; or (b) the superannuation provider
-- for the fund has not notified the Commissioner ... that the fund accepts New Zealand-sourced amounts." (2AAB): "Despite
-- paragraph (2)(d), the Commissioner must not pay the unclaimed money to the person if [it] includes a New Zealand-sourced
-- amount and the person has not reached the New Zealand eligibility age."
-- ss 20QF(2), 21E(2), 22B(2), 24G(2) have the same (a), (aa), (b) and (c), the same New Zealand rule for funds (20QF(2A),
-- 21E(2A), 22B(2A), 24G(2AA)), but (d) is narrower: "to the person if this paragraph applies", and it applies only if "(a)
-- subparagraphs (2)(a)(ii) and (aa)(ii) do not apply [no direction]; and (b) ... (i) the person has reached the eligibility age
-- and, if the amount includes a New Zealand-sourced amount, the New Zealand eligibility age; (ii) the amount is less than $200;
-- (iii) a terminal medical condition ... exists in relation to the person; and (c) the person has not died." (20QF(3), 21E(3),
-- 22B(3), 24G(2A).)
-- Reading (NOTES.md finding 4): a direction to a fund the New Zealand rule forbids is not "any other case" under s 17(2)(d);
-- the Commissioner cannot pay that fund and nothing is paid until I direct another. Under s 17(2), a direction to a fund that is
-- not a complying superannuation plan, or to a KiwiSaver provider whose prescribed matters are not met, leaves (a) or (aa)
-- unmet, so (d) applies and I am paid directly. Under ss 20QF etc a direction that fails leaves (d) unavailable, because (d)
-- needs no direction at all.
DECLARE `Where the Commissioner holds my money from` IS ONE OF
    `unclaimed money my fund paid under s 17(1)`
    `an inactive low-balance account my fund paid under s 20QD`
    `an eligible rollover fund account paid under s 21C`
    `a voluntary payment my fund made under s 22`
    `a lost member account my fund paid under s 24E`

DECLARE `What I have asked the Commissioner to do` IS ONE OF
    `I have directed payment to a single super fund`
    `I have directed payment to a single KiwiSaver scheme provider`
    `I have given no direction`

DECLARE `Whom the Commissioner must pay` IS ONE OF
    `the single fund I directed`
    `the single KiwiSaver scheme provider I directed`
    `the death beneficiaries, the share of each worked out by the formula (the whole amount if there is only one)`
    `the dead member's legal personal representative`
    `me, directly`
    `no one yet: the Commissioner is not satisfied that it is possible to pay in accordance with the Act`
    `no one yet: the Commissioner must not pay the fund I directed, because the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and that fund is a self managed fund or has not notified that it accepts such amounts`
    `no one yet: the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and I have not reached the New Zealand eligibility age, so it cannot be paid to me directly`
    `no one yet: I must direct the Commissioner to pay a complying super fund or a KiwiSaver provider, unless I reach eligibility age, the amount is under $200 or I have a terminal medical condition`

@export The ATO holds my super (unclaimed, inactive low-balance, ERF, voluntary or lost member money). Whom must the Commissioner pay it to?
GIVEN `where from` IS A `Where the Commissioner holds my money from` @desc Under which provision your fund paid the money to the Commissioner: unclaimed money (s 17), inactive low-balance (s 20QD), eligible rollover fund (s 21C), voluntary (s 22) or lost member account (s 24E)
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it can pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied, on your application in the approved form or on the Commissioner's own initiative, that it is possible to pay the money as the Act requires
      `the member has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the member whose money it is has died (answer no if it is your own and you are alive)
      `there are death beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the member has died: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the fund would have had to pay death benefits to one or more other people because of the death
      `my direction` IS A `What I have asked the Commissioner to do` @desc Whether you have directed the Commissioner to pay a single super fund, a single KiwiSaver scheme provider, or given no direction
      `the fund is a complying superannuation plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a super fund: whether it is a complying superannuation plan under the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997
      `the KiwiSaver prescribed matters are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a KiwiSaver provider: whether the matters the regulations prescribe (if any) are satisfied
      `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money includes an amount that came from a New Zealand KiwiSaver scheme
      `the fund is self managed or has not notified it accepts NZ amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a super fund: whether it is a self managed fund, or its trustee has not notified the Commissioner that it accepts New Zealand-sourced amounts
      `what my fund knows` IS A `What my fund knows of my sex` @desc Whether you are a man or a woman, as your fund knows it (it treats you as a man if it does not know)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in complete years
      `I have reached the New Zealand eligibility age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached New Zealand's superannuation eligibility age (only matters if the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount)
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Commissioner holds for you from this source, in dollars
      `I have a terminal medical condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a terminal medical condition within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 exists in relation to you
GIVETH A `Whom the Commissioner must pay`
`Whom must the Commissioner pay` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioner is satisfied it can pay`)
    THEN `no one yet: the Commissioner is not satisfied that it is possible to pay in accordance with the Act`
    ELSE IF `the member has died`
         THEN IF `there are death beneficiaries`
              THEN `the death beneficiaries, the share of each worked out by the formula (the whole amount if there is only one)`
              ELSE `the dead member's legal personal representative`
         ELSE IF `a direction is met`
              THEN IF `the direction is to a fund the NZ rule forbids`
                   THEN `no one yet: the Commissioner must not pay the fund I directed, because the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and that fund is a self managed fund or has not notified that it accepts such amounts`
                   ELSE `the payee directed`
              ELSE `paid to me, or not`
    WHERE
        `a direction is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my direction`
            WHEN `I have directed payment to a single super fund` THEN `the fund is a complying superannuation plan`
            WHEN `I have directed payment to a single KiwiSaver scheme provider` THEN `the KiwiSaver prescribed matters are met`
            WHEN `I have given no direction` THEN FALSE
        `the direction is to a fund the NZ rule forbids` MEANS
                `my direction` EQUALS `I have directed payment to a single super fund`
            AND `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount`
            AND `the fund is self managed or has not notified it accepts NZ amounts`
        `the payee directed` MEANS
            IF `my direction` EQUALS `I have directed payment to a single super fund`
            THEN `the single fund I directed`
            ELSE `the single KiwiSaver scheme provider I directed`
        `a New Zealand amount bars paying me` MEANS
            `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount` AND (NOT `I have reached the New Zealand eligibility age`)
        `paid to me, or not` MEANS
            IF `where from` EQUALS `unclaimed money my fund paid under s 17(1)`
            THEN IF `a New Zealand amount bars paying me`
                 THEN `no one yet: the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and I have not reached the New Zealand eligibility age, so it cannot be paid to me directly`
                 ELSE `me, directly`
            ELSE IF `my direction` EQUALS `I have given no direction`
                 THEN IF     (`I have reached the eligibility age` `what my fund knows` `my age` AND (NOT `a New Zealand amount bars paying me`))
                          OR `the amount` LESS THAN 200
                          OR `I have a terminal medical condition`
                      THEN `me, directly`
                      ELSE `no one yet: I must direct the Commissioner to pay a complying super fund or a KiwiSaver provider, unless I reach eligibility age, the amount is under $200 or I have a terminal medical condition`
                 ELSE `no one yet: I must direct the Commissioner to pay a complying super fund or a KiwiSaver provider, unless I reach eligibility age, the amount is under $200 or I have a terminal medical condition`

-- The death beneficiaries' shares (ss 17(2AA), 20QF(4), 21E(4), 22B(4), 24G(3)): "the amount worked out using the following
-- formula:" -- the formula is missing from the deposited text. The note says: "If there is only one death beneficiary, the
-- whole of the amount is payable to that beneficiary."
@export A member has died and the ATO holds their super for the death beneficiaries. How much is my share as a death beneficiary?
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Commissioner holds for the member who died, in dollars
      `the number of death beneficiaries` IS A NUMBER @desc How many death beneficiaries the Commissioner is satisfied there are
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much is my share as a death beneficiary` MEANS
    IF `the number of death beneficiaries` EQUALS 1
    THEN `answered` `the amount`
    ELSE `not covered` `the death-beneficiary formula is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so a share cannot be worked out where there is more than one death beneficiary`

§§ `ss 17(2AB)-(2AE), 20QF(5)-(6), 21E(5)-(6), 22B(5)-(6), 24G(3A)-(3D) -- is interest paid with it`

-- s 17(2AB), (2AC): if the Commissioner makes a payment "on or after 1 July 2013", the Commissioner "must also pay ... the
-- amount of interest (if any) worked out in accordance with the regulations"; (2AE): no interest "in relation to a period
-- before 1 July 2013". s 24G(3A), (3B), (3D): the same, from 1 July 2013. ss 20QF(5), (6), 21E(5), (6), 22B(5), (6): "must
-- also pay ... the amount of interest (if any) worked out in accordance with the regulations", with no date. The rate (which
-- may be nil, ss 17(2AD), 20QF(7)) is the regulations', not deposited: the answer says whether interest is due, not how much.
@export When the ATO pays my super back, must it also pay me interest?
GIVEN `where from` IS A `Where the Commissioner holds my money from` @desc Under which provision your fund paid the money to the Commissioner: unclaimed money (s 17), inactive low-balance (s 20QD), eligible rollover fund (s 21C), voluntary (s 22) or lost member account (s 24E)
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner pays the money out
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner also pay interest` IF
    IF     `where from` EQUALS `unclaimed money my fund paid under s 17(1)`
        OR `where from` EQUALS `a lost member account my fund paid under s 24E`
    THEN `the day of payment` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2013
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `s 20H -- former temporary resident: getting my super back`

-- (Situation: my super went to the Commissioner because I left Australia after a temporary visa.)
-- s 20H(1): it applies if the Commissioner is satisfied, on application or own initiative, that "(a) either: (i) the person
-- has been identified in a notice under section 20C; or (ii) the person was ... the holder of a temporary visa, except a visa
-- prescribed by the regulations, that ceased to be in effect at least 6 months ago, and the person left Australia at least 6
-- months ago but after starting to be the holder of the visa; and (b)" the amounts paid to the Commissioner for the person
-- exceed the amounts the Commissioner has paid out.
-- (2): "The Commissioner must pay the excess: (a) to the person; or (b) to a single fund that is a complying superannuation
-- plan ..., if the person directs the Commissioner to pay to the fund and the Commissioner is satisfied that the person is: (i)
-- an Australian citizen; or (ii) a New Zealand citizen; or (iii) ... the holder of a permanent visa or a visa prescribed by the
-- regulations; or (ba) to a single KiwiSaver scheme provider, if the person directs ... and the matters (if any) prescribed by
-- the regulations are satisfied; or (c) to the person's legal personal representative, if the person has died." (2AAA): the
-- same New Zealand rule for funds. (3): if the person has died and there are death beneficiaries, the Commissioner "must pay
-- each death beneficiary". (6): payment is subject to Division 12 in Schedule 1 to the TAA (withholding from a departing
-- Australia superannuation payment; not encoded).
-- Reading: (a) is the default where (b), (ba) and (c) do not apply.
DECLARE `Whom the Commissioner must pay under s 20H` IS ONE OF
    `me, directly (s 20H(2)(a)), less any tax withheld from a departing Australia superannuation payment`
    `the single complying super fund I directed (s 20H(2)(b))`
    `the single KiwiSaver scheme provider I directed (s 20H(2)(ba))`
    `the death beneficiaries (s 20H(3))`
    `the dead person's legal personal representative (s 20H(2)(c))`
    `no one yet: the Commissioner must not pay the fund I directed, because the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and that fund is a self managed fund or has not notified that it accepts such amounts (s 20H(2AAA))`
    `no one: s 20H does not apply on these facts`

@export My super went to the ATO after I left Australia on a temporary visa. Whom must the Commissioner pay it to (s 20H)?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied, on your application or of the Commissioner's own initiative, that you were named in a s 20C notice, or held a non-prescribed temporary visa that ceased at least 6 months ago and left Australia at least 6 months ago after it began
      `the Commissioner holds an excess for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amounts paid to the Commissioner for you exceed what the Commissioner has already paid out for you
      `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person whose super it is has died
      `there are death beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person has died: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the funds would have had to pay death benefits to one or more other people
      `my direction` IS A `What I have asked the Commissioner to do` @desc Whether you have directed the Commissioner to pay a single super fund, a single KiwiSaver scheme provider, or given no direction
      `the fund is a complying superannuation plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a super fund: whether it is a complying superannuation plan
      `I am a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a super fund: whether the Commissioner is satisfied you are an Australian or New Zealand citizen, or hold a permanent visa (or a visa the regulations prescribe)
      `the KiwiSaver prescribed matters are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a KiwiSaver provider: whether the matters the regulations prescribe (if any) are satisfied
      `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money includes an amount that came from a New Zealand KiwiSaver scheme
      `the fund is self managed or has not notified it accepts NZ amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you directed a super fund: whether it is self managed, or has not notified the Commissioner that it accepts New Zealand-sourced amounts
GIVETH A `Whom the Commissioner must pay under s 20H`
`Whom must the Commissioner pay under s 20H` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioner is satisfied`) OR (NOT `the Commissioner holds an excess for me`)
    THEN `no one: s 20H does not apply on these facts`
    ELSE IF `the person has died`
         THEN IF `there are death beneficiaries`
              THEN `the death beneficiaries (s 20H(3))`
              ELSE `the dead person's legal personal representative (s 20H(2)(c))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `my direction`
              WHEN `I have directed payment to a single super fund` THEN
                  IF `the fund is a complying superannuation plan` AND `I am a citizen or permanent resident`
                  THEN IF `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount` AND `the fund is self managed or has not notified it accepts NZ amounts`
                       THEN `no one yet: the Commissioner must not pay the fund I directed, because the money includes a New Zealand-sourced amount and that fund is a self managed fund or has not notified that it accepts such amounts (s 20H(2AAA))`
                       ELSE `the single complying super fund I directed (s 20H(2)(b))`
                  ELSE `me, directly (s 20H(2)(a)), less any tax withheld from a departing Australia superannuation payment`
              WHEN `I have directed payment to a single KiwiSaver scheme provider` THEN
                  IF `the KiwiSaver prescribed matters are met`
                  THEN `the single KiwiSaver scheme provider I directed (s 20H(2)(ba))`
                  ELSE `me, directly (s 20H(2)(a)), less any tax withheld from a departing Australia superannuation payment`
              WHEN `I have given no direction` THEN `me, directly (s 20H(2)(a)), less any tax withheld from a departing Australia superannuation payment`

§§ `s 24NA -- will the ATO move it into my active account`

-- s 24NA(1): it applies if the Commissioner holds a "superannuation amount" for me (paid under s 17(1), 20QD, 21C, 22 or 24E,
-- after applying s 20H), and "(b) the Commissioner is satisfied, on application in the approved form or on the Commissioner's
-- own initiative, that it is possible ... to pay the superannuation amount in accordance with subsection (2)". (1A): the
-- Commissioner "must pay ... within 28 days after the Commissioner is satisfied". (2): to a single fund if "(a) the person has
-- not died; and (b) the superannuation provider for the fund holds an account on behalf of the person in the fund; and (c) [it]
-- has received an amount in respect of the person during the prescribed period; and (d) the balance of the account will be
-- equal to or greater than $6,000 if all of the superannuation amounts in respect of the person are paid into the account; and
-- (e) ... the fund can accept payment ...; and (f) [for a New Zealand-sourced amount] either: (i) the fund is not self managed
-- superannuation fund; or (ii) the superannuation provider for the fund has notified the Commissioner ... that the fund accepts
-- New Zealand-sourced amounts." (3): more than one such fund: "in accordance with the regulations" (not covered). (4):
-- interest worked out under the regulations is also paid to the fund. "Within 28 days after": by the day of satisfaction plus
-- 28.
DECLARE `Will the ATO move my money to my active account` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commissioner must pay it into that account, with any interest the regulations give` HAS `by` IS A DATE
    `no: s 24NA does not require the Commissioner to pay it into that account`

@export Will the ATO move the super it holds for me into my active super account (s 24NA), and by when?
GIVEN `the Commissioner holds super for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner holds an amount for you that a fund paid as unclaimed money, from an inactive low-balance, eligible rollover fund or lost member account, or voluntarily
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it can pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied, on your application or of the Commissioner's own initiative, that it is possible to pay it into your active account
      `the day the Commissioner was satisfied` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner became satisfied that it could pay it
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the member has died
      `my fund holds an account for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your active fund holds an account on your behalf
      `my fund received an amount for me in the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that fund received an amount for you (a contribution or rollover) during the period the regulations prescribe
      `the account balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The balance of that account now, in dollars
      `the total the ATO holds for me` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all the amounts the Commissioner holds for you, in dollars
      `the fund can accept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund's terms and Commonwealth law let it accept the payment for you
      `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money includes an amount from a New Zealand KiwiSaver scheme
      `the fund is self managed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the active fund is a self managed superannuation fund
      `the fund has notified it accepts NZ amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund's trustee has notified the Commissioner that the fund accepts New Zealand-sourced amounts
      `another fund also qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a second fund also holds an active account for you that meets the same tests
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Will the ATO move my money to my active account`
`Will the ATO move my money to my active account (s 24NA)` MEANS
    IF     `the Commissioner holds super for me`
       AND `the Commissioner is satisfied it can pay`
       AND (NOT `I have died`)
       AND `the fund tests are met`
    THEN IF `another fund also qualifies`
         THEN `not covered` `more than one fund meets s 24NA(2)(b) to (e), so the Commissioner pays as the regulations provide (s 24NA(3)), and the regulations are not deposited`
         ELSE `answered` (`yes: the Commissioner must pay it into that account, with any interest the regulations give` (`the day the Commissioner was satisfied` PLUS 28))
    ELSE `answered` `no: s 24NA does not require the Commissioner to pay it into that account`
    WHERE
        `the fund tests are met` MEANS
                `my fund holds an account for me`
            AND `my fund received an amount for me in the prescribed period`
            AND (`the account balance` PLUS `the total the ATO holds for me`) AT LEAST 6000
            AND `the fund can accept it`
            AND (    (NOT `it includes a New Zealand-sourced amount`)
                  OR (NOT `the fund is self managed`)
                  OR `the fund has notified it accepts NZ amounts`)

§§ `ss 20L, 20QK, 21G, 22E, 24K, 24NAA -- can the ATO take back an overpayment from me`

-- (Situation: the Commissioner paid me more than was properly payable.)
-- s 24K (and the same words in ss 20L, 20QK, 21G, 22E): if the Commissioner pays more than "properly payable", the
-- Commissioner "may recover all or part of the excess from ... (a) the person to whom the payment was made (whether ... in his
-- or her own right or as the legal personal representative ...)", "if ... (a) the Commissioner gave the debtor written notice,
-- as prescribed by the regulations, of the proposed recovery and the amount to be recovered; and (b) at least 28 days have
-- passed since the notice was given; and (c) the amount recovered is not more than the amount specified in the notice." (6): the
-- notice may be revoked. (7): "The total of the amounts recovered from different debtors in relation to the same excess must
-- not be more than the excess." A payment to a KiwiSaver scheme provider is excluded.
-- s 24NAA: an overpayment under Part 4B (a transfer to my active account) may be recovered only from the superannuation
-- provider, never from me (s 24NAA(3)).
-- "at least 28 days have passed since the notice was given": from the day of the notice plus 28.
DECLARE `How I was overpaid` IS ONE OF
    `paid to me, or to me as legal personal representative, under Part 3, 3A, 3B, 3C, 3D or 4A`
    `paid into my active account under s 24NA`

@export The ATO paid me too much of my super back. How much can it now recover from me as a debt?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I was overpaid` @desc Whether the overpayment was paid to you (or to you as executor or administrator) or was a transfer into your active super account under s 24NA
      `the excess` IS A NUMBER @desc How much more the Commissioner paid than was properly payable, in dollars
      `I was given a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given you written notice of the proposed recovery and the amount
      `the notice was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has revoked that notice
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given to you
      `the amount in the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the notice says will be recovered, in dollars
      `already recovered from others` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the same excess has already been recovered from anyone else (a super fund), in dollars
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can the ATO now recover from me` MEANS
    IF     `how` EQUALS `paid to me, or to me as legal personal representative, under Part 3, 3A, 3B, 3C, 3D or 4A`
       AND `I was given a notice`
       AND (NOT `the notice was revoked`)
       AND `today` AT LEAST (`the day of the notice` PLUS 28)
    THEN max 0 (min `the amount in the notice` (`the excess` MINUS `already recovered from others`))
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 20P -- can I object`

-- s 20P: "A person who is dissatisfied with a notice given, or a decision made, by the Commissioner in the administration of
-- Division 2, 4 or 5 of this Part [Part 3A] may object against the notice or decision in the manner set out in Part IVC of the
-- Taxation Administration Act 1953." Division 2 is s 20C (notices), Division 4 is s 20H (payment), Division 5 is ss 20J-20M
-- (revocation, refunds, recovery). No other provision of this Act gives an objection or review (NOTES.md finding 7); other
-- review rights, if any, are outside this Act.
DECLARE `The Commissioner's decision` IS ONE OF
    `a notice to my fund that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)`
    `a decision about paying me, or refusing my application, under s 20H`
    `a decision to revoke, or not revoke, a s 20C notice (s 20J)`
    `a decision to recover an overpayment of my s 20H payment (s 20L)`
    `a decision about unclaimed money, an inactive low-balance, ERF, voluntary or lost member amount (ss 17, 20QF, 21E, 22B, 24G)`
    `a decision to recover an overpayment under ss 20QK, 21G, 22E or 24K`
    `a decision about transferring my money to my active account (s 24NA)`

DECLARE `Can I object` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may object under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (s 20P)`
    `this Act gives no right to object to that decision`

@export Can I object to the Commissioner's decision about my super under this Act?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The Commissioner's decision` @desc Which decision of the Commissioner you are unhappy with
GIVETH A `Can I object`
`Can I object to the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a notice to my fund that I am a former temporary resident (s 20C)` THEN `yes: I may object under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (s 20P)`
    WHEN `a decision about paying me, or refusing my application, under s 20H` THEN `yes: I may object under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (s 20P)`
    WHEN `a decision to revoke, or not revoke, a s 20C notice (s 20J)` THEN `yes: I may object under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (s 20P)`
    WHEN `a decision to recover an overpayment of my s 20H payment (s 20L)` THEN `yes: I may object under Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (s 20P)`
    OTHERWISE `this Act gives no right to object to that decision`
